                <m3e-tabs class="recipe-tabs" p-on:change="selectPanel">
                    <m3e-tab active>Ingredients</m3e-tab>
                    <m3e-tab>Method</m3e-tab>
                    <m3e-tab>Nutrition</m3e-tab>
                    <m3e-tab>Reviews (7)</m3e-tab>
                </m3e-tabs>

                <!-- Ingredients -->
                <section class="recipe-panel" p-ref="panel0" aria-label="Ingredients">
                    <div class="panel-header">
                        <h2 class="subsection-title">Ingredients</h2>
                        <div class="servings-control">
                            <span id="servings-label">Servings</span>
                            <m3e-slider class="servings-slider"
                                        discrete
                                        min="1"
                                        max="12"
                                        value="4"
                                        step="1"
                                        aria-labelledby="servings-label"
                                        p-on:change="changeServings"></m3e-slider>
                            <strong p-ref="servingsValue">4</strong>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div p-ref="ingredients">
                        <m3e-list>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="450" data-unit="g">450g</span> halloumi, cut into 2cm cubes</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="2">2</span> courgettes, sliced into thick ribbons</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="250" data-unit="g">250g</span> cherry tomatoes on the vine</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="3" data-unit="tbsp">3 tbsp</span> olive oil</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="1" data-unit="tbsp">1 tbsp</span> dried oregano</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="1">1</span> unwaxed lemon, zest and juice</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="2" data-unit="tbsp">2 tbsp</span> honey</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient">A large handful of fresh mint, roughly torn</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient">Chilli flakes, to taste</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient">Flatbreads, to serve</span></m3e-list-item>
                        </m3e-list>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Method -->
                <section class="recipe-panel" p-ref="panel1" aria-label="Method" hidden>
                    <h2 class="subsection-title">Method</h2>
                    <ol class="step-list">
                        <li>Pat the halloumi dry with kitchen paper. This is not optional and we will not be taking questions. Wet halloumi steams instead of browning, and a steamed halloumi is a sad, pale thing that has let everybody down. Dry it properly and it will reward you with a crust.</li>
                        <li>Toss the halloumi, courgette and tomatoes with the olive oil and oregano. Thread onto skewers, alternating as the mood takes you. There is no correct order. The mice have argued about this for years and reached no conclusion.</li>
                        <li>Get a griddle pan properly, alarmingly hot. Lay the skewers down and then leave them alone for three minutes. Do not poke. Do not fuss. Do not turn them &ldquo;just to check&rdquo;. The crust forms in the stillness. This is the whole secret of the dish and possibly of life.</li>
                        <li>Turn once, give them another three minutes, and listen for the squeak. Halloumi squeaks against the tooth, which is the noise of a cheese that knows exactly what it is doing. Fresh from the pan it squeaks loudest.</li>
                        <li>Whisk the lemon juice and zest with the honey and pour it over the hot skewers so it hisses and catches. Scatter the mint and chilli flakes, pile onto warm flatbreads, and serve at once. Halloumi waits for nobody. Ten minutes cold and it turns to rubber, so eat it standing up if you have to. We usually do.</li>
                    </ol>
                </section>

                <!-- Nutrition -->
                <section class="recipe-panel" p-ref="panel2" aria-label="Nutrition" hidden>
                    <h2 class="subsection-title">Nutrition (per serving)</h2>
                    <ul class="nutrition-list">
                            <li class="nutrition-row"><span class="nutrition-label">Calories</span><span class="nutrition-value">410 kcal</span></li>
