            </article>

            <!-- Squeak peek bottom sheet -->
            <m3e-bottom-sheet p-ref="tipsSheet" modal>
                <h2 class="subsection-title">Squeak peek: cooking tips</h2>
                <m3e-list>
                    <m3e-list-item>Soak wooden skewers for twenty minutes first, or they will char faster than the cheese does and everyone will pretend not to notice.</m3e-list-item>
                    <m3e-list-item>Halloumi is already salty, so hold the salt until the very end and taste before you reach for it. The lemon does most of the seasoning work anyway.</m3e-list-item>
                    <m3e-list-item>No griddle pan? A heavy frying pan works, and so does a barbecue. What matters is the heat, not the hardware.</m3e-list-item>
                </m3e-list>
            </m3e-bottom-sheet>

            <!-- Cheese fact dialog -->
            <m3e-dialog p-ref="cheeseFact" headline="Cheese fact!">
                <p class="prose">Halloumi comes from Cyprus, where it has been made since at least the medieval period. Its high melting point comes from the way the curds are heated before brining, which is why it grills instead of running away.</p>
                <m3e-button variant="filled" slot="actions" p-on:click="closeCheeseFact">Gouda to know!</m3e-button>
            </m3e-dialog>

            <!-- Snackbar -->
            <m3e-snackbar p-ref="snackbar"></m3e-snackbar>

